    "body": "US President Donald Trump speaks during the United Nations General Assembly (UNGA) in New York, US, on Tuesday, Sept. 22, 2026. (Photographer: Angelina Katsanis/Bloomberg via Getty Images)\nWASHINGTON — President Donald Trump will give a keynote speech at the annual Reagan National Defense Forum, becoming the first president to speak at the event.\nTrump’s speech is scheduled for 3:00 p.m. Pacific Standard Time on Friday Dec. 4. The vast majority of Reagan’s programming is held the next day, meaning Trump will have a solo spotlight to address the crowd.\nThe RNDF, held at the Reagan Presidential Library in Simi Valley, Calif., has steadily grown as a key defense event year over year. While drawing leadership from the Pentagon and traditional defense industry, it has emerged as the hub for the California-based defense tech startup scene — of which many have politically aligned themselves with the Trump administration.\nTrump’s speech could provide an interesting contrast to the main day programing, where democratic lawmakers are expected to appear on panels and do interviews outlining their plans for the new Congress.\nBreaking Defense Video\nCandidates are lining up to be the next top HASC Republican.\nWatch Now »\nThe real-world missile defense lessons from Ukraine and Iran — and how they matter for China\nWatch Now »\nA $1.1 trillion Pentagon budget plan sets up a fight on Capitol Hill\nWatch Now »\nThe Pentagon fails another audit. Can it turn things around by 2028?\nWatch Now »\nA new Air Force stunt plane, plus a shakeup for special operations\nWatch Now »\nNATO nations have a missile crisis. How did it happen, and can it be fixed?\nWatch Now »\nA Pentagon impeachment showdown, plus defense funding in limbo\nWatch Now »\npresented by\nThe push to give dismounted forces direct access to LEO and MEO networks [Sponsored]\nWatch Now »\nThe Pentagon wants a massive new military base. Where will it go?\nWatch Now »\nWhat now? Budget fight, Hegseth impeachment on deck for defense-focused lawmakers after midterms\nWatch Now »\nScroll for more video",
